From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mxml: skip leading whitespace before the SOAP root element

init_xml() calls mxmlLoadString() with a NULL top. mxml_load_data() then
requires the very first byte to be '<':

    else if (ch != '<' && !top) {
        _mxml_error(options, "XML does not start with '<' (saw '%c').", ch);
        return (NULL);
    }

A SOAP body that begins with whitespace and no XML declaration is valid
XML, but fails that check, so the whole request is rejected with a
ter:InvalidArgVal "Malformed request" fault. ZoneMinder's ONVIF control
module sends exactly that shape, which broke every PTZ command against
the camera.

Reproduced against the linked mxml 4.0.4: a body starting with "\n    "
returns NULL from mxmlLoadString(), while the identical body parses once
the leading whitespace is skipped.

Skip leading whitespace before handing the buffer to mxmlLoadString().
get_method() already skips non-element siblings, so the Envelope and Body
are still located.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

--- a/src/mxml_wrapper.c
+++ b/src/mxml_wrapper.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include "string.h"
 #include "utils.h"
 
+#include <ctype.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
 // In mxml v4, mxmlLoadString returns a document node, not the root element
@@ -56,7 +57,15 @@
     memcpy(tmp_buf, buffer, (size_t) buffer_size);
     tmp_buf[buffer_size] = '\0';
 
-    doc_xml = mxmlLoadString(NULL, NULL, tmp_buf);
+    // mxmlLoadString() with a NULL top rejects a document that does not start
+    // with '<' (mxml_load_data()), but SOAP clients such as ZoneMinder send a
+    // body that begins with whitespace and no XML declaration. Skip it so the
+    // Envelope is still found.
+    char *xml_start = tmp_buf;
+    while (isspace((unsigned char) *xml_start))
+        xml_start++;
+
+    doc_xml = mxmlLoadString(NULL, NULL, xml_start);
     free(tmp_buf);
     if (!doc_xml) {
         log_error("Failed to parse XML string - mxmlLoadString returned NULL");
